\subsubsection{Integration Tests}

The integration tests exercise the complete Phase 4 pipeline: block assembly,
hash verification, and disk writing. These tests use [[InProgressPiece]] from
the pieces module to simulate real download scenarios where blocks arrive out
of order.

\begin{itemize}
\item \textbf{Multi-file with out-of-order blocks}: Creates a 3-file torrent
  (80 + 60 + 60 = 200 bytes) with 64-byte pieces. Tests receiving blocks for
  a piece that spans file boundaries, verifying the hash, writing to disk,
  and reading back to confirm correctness.

\item \textbf{Multi-block piece out-of-order}: Uses a 40,000-byte piece (3
  blocks at 16,384 bytes each) to test block assembly when blocks arrive in
  reverse order (2, 0, 1). Verifies the complete pipeline from block reception
  through disk read-back.

\item \textbf{Piece spanning two files}: Focused test on the file boundary
